* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call !tkkeys(op, keys, a, b, c, d, e)         ALWAYS SEVEN ARGUMENTS: a call with fewer stops with "Argument count mismatch" (pad with '')
*
*   The ops are $tk_keys's: add, name, action, menu, why, menus, keyof and keylist.  The table runs nothing: a handler is the program's own CASE on the action id.
*   The two ops that offer an action to the AI (ai, aiacts) do nothing here: the AI line is not part of this library, and aiacts answers nothing.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tkkeys(op, keys, a, b, c, d, e)
$catalog !tkkeys

   if op = 'aiacts' then
      b = ''
      c = ''
   end else
      if op # 'ai' then call $tk_keys(op, keys, a, b, c, d, e)
   end
   return
end

* END-CODE
